// Rule: [T1003.002][T1003.005] Interlock - Volatility Credential Plugins
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1003.002, T1003.005
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Behavioral candidate for Volatility3 plugins that extract SAM hashes or cached domain credentials from a Windows memory image.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for volatility credential plugins using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A process requested a Volatility3 plugin designed to extract local or cached domain credential material and requires immediate authorization review.
// A match does not prove: Successful extraction, valid credentials, malicious operator, follow-on access, ransomware deployment or Interlock attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Interlock - Volatility credential-extraction plugins
// Classification: Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
//
// Sophos EIR directly observed both plugin invocations in an Interlock intrusion.
// The plugin strings describe SAM hash extraction and cached domain credential
// extraction. Do not suppress approved DFIR activity by filename alone: validate
// the actor, device, case/change record, memory image provenance and execution time.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "windows.hashdump.Hashdump"
    or ProcessCommandLine contains "windows.cachedump.Cachedump"
| project Timestamp,
          DeviceId,
          DeviceName,
          AccountDomain,
          AccountName,
          FileName,
          FolderPath,
          ProcessCommandLine,
          ProcessIntegrityLevel,
          ProcessTokenElevation,
          ProcessUniqueId,
          InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessUniqueId,
          SHA1,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
